{"abstract":[{"text":"The trill-sound attribute group includes attributes used to guide the sound of trills, mordents, turns,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"shakes, and wavy lines. The default choices are:","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"trillSound","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTrillSound","text":"MXLTrillSound","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL13MXLTrillSoundV"}],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"discussion","level":2,"text":"Discussion","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Start-Note = “upper” trill-step = “whole” two-note-turn = “none” accelerate = “no” beats = “4”.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Second-beat and last-beat are percentages for landing on the indicated beat, with defaults of 25 and 75","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"respectively.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"For mordent and inverted-mordent elements, the defaults are different:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The default start-note is “main”, not “upper”. The default for beats is “3”, not “4”. The default for second-","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"beat is “12”, not “25”. The default for last-beat is “24”, not “75”.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLWavyLine\/trillSound"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLWavyLine"]]},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlwavyline\/trillsound"],"traits":[{"inte